# Integrity-critical paths.  This file documents ownership and makes GitHub
# auto-request the owner on pull requests that touch these paths.  It is NOT the
# merge gate: the gate is the signed referee check required by the branch ruleset
# (a solo owner cannot approve their own pull requests, so Code Owner review is
# deliberately not required).  Changes to the paths below fail the referee
# (PROTECTED_PATH_MODIFIED) and need the owner to relax the ruleset for that merge.
# (See canonical/governance/REPO_INTEGRITY_POLICY_V1.json, section github_side.)

# The guard itself, its test, the referee workflow, the landing script, and this file
/execution_guard/                                   @moxnixmdj
/.github/scripts/land_on_main.sh                    @moxnixmdj
/canonical/tests/test_repo_integrity_guard_v1.py    @moxnixmdj
/.github/                                           @moxnixmdj
/AGENTS.md                                          @moxnixmdj

# Test infrastructure (a conftest.py was used to serve historical bytes to 184 tests)
/canonical/tests/conftest.py                        @moxnixmdj
/tests/conftest.py                                  @moxnixmdj
/conftest.py                                        @moxnixmdj

# Terminal truth and its mirrors
/canonical/CANONICAL_POINTER.json                   @moxnixmdj
/canonical/governance/                              @moxnixmdj
/canonical/capabilities/frontier/                   @moxnixmdj
/canonical/capabilities/opus55/                     @moxnixmdj
/canonical/runtime/BOUND_CAPABILITY_REGISTRY_V1.json @moxnixmdj

# The honest suite baseline and the tool that writes it
/canonical/verification/HONEST_SUITE_BASELINE_20261014_V1.json @moxnixmdj
